    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0680" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1830: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nouméa (MacVitty) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nouméa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-05T17:00:00+11:00">February 5, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 5—2:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. The Australian Intelligence officer here today, informed me that a radio
                    message from the Japanese Commissioner at Hanoi to Tokyo intercepted by his
                    service reads: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Admiral Decoux<anchor n="54" xml:id="d665-f1"/> has agreed to cooperate
                            with the Japanese in taking possession of all French territory in the
                            Pacific with the understanding that French sovereignty will be
                            preserved.[”]</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0681" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/>
                <p>In this connection d’Argenlieu<anchor n="55" xml:id="d665-f2"/> recently gave me
                    to understand that he believed the State Department had come to some agreement
                    with Vichy whereby no protection would be given by the United States to French
                    possessions in the Pacific. He inferred that this belief was also shared by
                    General de Gaulle.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d665-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d665-f1" n="54" xml:id="d665-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. Jean Decoux, Governor General of Indochina and High Commissioner for French
                    Possessions in the Pacific.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d665-f2" n="55" xml:id="d665-f2-content">
                <p>Thierry d’Argenlieu, Free French High Commissioner for the Pacific.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d665-f3" n="56" xml:id="d665-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Charles de Gaulle, President of the National Committee of the Free French at
                    London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
